# Local settings for development and server runtime. Copy to docker/.env (not versioned) and edit as needed:
#   cp docker/.env.example docker/.env
#
# Used during compilation/configuration and at server runtime:
# - docker/build.sh loads this file and passes X2_* values to CMake; CMake writes template settings into dist/.
# - docker/server/docker-compose.yml loads this file into server containers when they start.
# - Docker Compose and restore.sh also read the development database settings below.
# Values baked into dist/ take effect after reconfiguring/rebuilding. At runtime, only settings read from the process environment
# can override them (such as the resource paths). Compose service-level environment values take precedence over this file.
# Shell variables take precedence for scripts/builds. Use plain KEY=VALUE lines (no quotes or `export`).
# CMake input paths are relative to the repository root; server resource paths are relative to each server directory.
# Details: docs/tools/development-database.md, docs/tools/runtime.md, docs/tools/build-environment.md.

# --- Build-only variables ---
# Build-only variables
## Package destination. Defaults to dist/ at the repository root; all presets use the same path.
X2_DIST_DIR=dist
## Client data directory containing data*.kom files used to generate ClientScript.
X2_CLIENT_DATA=_client/data
# ----------------------------

# --- Development database (Docker Compose and restore.sh) ---
# SQL Server sa password. SQL Server reads it when its data volume is created. To change it later, remove the volume
# (`docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml down -v`) and restore the databases again.
X2_DB_PASSWORD=X2dev!Passw0rd
# Host port published on 127.0.0.1. Used as the default port in X2_DB_SERVER.
X2_DB_PORT=1433
# Address announced by servers and written by restore.sh to LServerList/LChannelList; clients connect to this address.
X2_SERVER_IP=127.0.0.1

# --- Package defaults (CMake; written into dist/) ---
# Database connection used in generated .dsn files. X2_DB_SERVER overrides the host and port default above.
X2_DB_SERVER=127.0.0.1,1433
X2_DB_USER=sa
# Optional ODBC driver and options. By default, CMake uses FreeTDS if found, otherwise ODBC Driver 18.
# For host runs, set the driver path installed on the host (for example, /usr/lib/libtdsodbc.so on Arch).
#X2_ODBC_DRIVER=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/odbc/libtdsodbc.so
#X2_ODBC_OPTIONS=TDS_Version=7.4;ClientCharset=UTF-8
# EPublisherServer listen port and the URL other servers use to reach it.
X2_EPUBLISHER_PORT=8000
X2_EPUBLISHER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/
# Default paths for server configs. Server processes can override these at runtime with the same environment variables.
X2_SERVERRESOURCE_DIR=../ServerResource
X2_CLIENTSCRIPT_DIR=../ClientScript

# --- Tests ---
# ODBC connection string (without DATABASE) enables the database suite of x2_server_common_tests.
#X2_TEST_ODBC=DRIVER=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/odbc/libtdsodbc.so;SERVER=127.0.0.1,1433;UID=sa;PWD=X2dev!Passw0rd;TDS_Version=7.4;ClientCharset=UTF-8

# --- Build container (docker/build.sh) ---
#X2_BUILD_IMAGE=x2-build
# Container home directory for the ccache cache (absolute path; `~` is not expanded).
#X2_BUILD_HOME=/home/user/.cache/x2-build

# --- Windows test machine (tools/win/winbuild.sh) ---
#X2_WIN_HOST=user@host
#X2_WIN_DIR=C:/x2
